## What Problem This Solves

`truncateFallbackReasonPart()` in `src/auto-reply/fallback-state.ts` uses raw `text.slice(0, max - 1)` to truncate fallback error reason text displayed to users. When `FALLBACK_REASON_PART_MAX = 80` and an emoji (UTF-16 surrogate pair) sits exactly at positions 78-79, `slice(0, 79)` leaves a dangling high surrogate — producing garbled `�` in fallback notices like `↪️ Model Fallback: ...`.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replace `text.slice(0, Math.max(0, max - 1))` with `truncateUtf16Safe(text, max - 1)`. The `truncateUtf16Safe` helper drops the lone high surrogate instead of splitting the surrogate pair, keeping the displayed text intact.

Same pattern as the 20+ already-merged UTF-16 truncation PRs (#102496, #102087, #101654, #102246, etc.).

## User Impact

Fallback model notices (`↪️ Model Fallback: ...`) with emoji near the reason text boundary no longer display garbled `�` characters.

## Evidence

**Real environment tested:** local OpenClaw source checkout, Node v24.13.1, PR head.

```
$ node --import tsx -e "
import { truncateUtf16Safe } from '@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice';

const FALLBACK_REASON_PART_MAX = 80;
const before = (v, max) => v.slice(0, Math.max(0, max - 1)).trimEnd();
const after = (v, max) => truncateUtf16Safe(v, max - 1).trimEnd();

const s79 = 'x'.repeat(78) + '😀';
console.log('Input: len=' + s79.length);

console.log('');
console.log('=== BEFORE (raw .slice) ===');
const b1 = before(s79, FALLBACK_REASON_PART_MAX);
console.log('len=' + b1.length, 'lone surrogate=' + (b1.charCodeAt(b1.length-1) >= 0xD800));

console.log('');
console.log('=== AFTER (truncateUtf16Safe) ===');
const a1 = after(s79, FALLBACK_REASON_PART_MAX);
console.log('len=' + a1.length, 'lone surrogate=' + (a1.charCodeAt(a1.length-1) >= 0xD800));
"
Input: len=80

=== BEFORE (raw .slice) ===
len=79 lone surrogate=true

=== AFTER (truncateUtf16Safe) ===
len=78 lone surrogate=false
```

**Observed result after fix:** Before fix, emoji at the 78-79 boundary produces a lone high surrogate (79 chars of broken text). After fix, `truncateUtf16Safe` drops the lone surrogate and returns 78 chars of intact text. Normal text without emoji at the boundary is unchanged.

**What was not tested:** Live Gateway end-to-end fallback notice rendering. The fix is a direct helper swap at a static boundary value (80); the helper's surrogate-safe behavior is proven independently.

## Regression Test Plan

- `$ npx oxlint src/auto-reply/fallback-state.ts` — **0 errors** ✅
- `$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/fallback-state.test.ts --run` — **1 passed, 15 tests passed** ✅
- `$ git diff --stat` — **1 file, +3/-2** ✅

## Root Cause

In `truncateFallbackReasonPart()`, `text.slice(0, Math.max(0, max - 1))` operates on UTF-16 code units. When `FALLBACK_REASON_PART_MAX - 1 = 79` (odd) and an emoji sits at positions 78-79, the high surrogate (index 78) is included but the low surrogate (index 79) is cut. The fix uses `truncateUtf16Safe` which detects the split surrogate pair and adjusts the boundary.

